## Ice Cream Sundae

Ice Cream Sundae is a fabric-based client pack I've put together and
occasionally update.

I haven't really used an unmodified client since... before 2020. In that time
I've grown rather attached to a selection of mods even when playing on vanilla
servers and made a habit of building a custom modlist whenever I boot up a new
version of minecraft. Then I figured that since I was putting together all this
stuff anyway, I may as well make it public. Even if only one person gets good
use from it, that's more return for work I was already doing. (fool that I was,
not knowing how much work that added)

So I put together [Ice Cream Sundae](https://modrinth.com/project/9jIRcx30) and
[Ice Cream Mondae](https://modrinth.com/project/Dl1zzMv5) (a version sans the
more graphics intensive features). Built around a core of mods like
[Accurate Block Placement](https://modrinth.com/project/kzwxhsjp),
[Mouse Tweaks](https://modrinth.com/project/aC3cM3Vq), client sorting,
clickthrough, and so on. Why there isn't already a pack combining these mods, I
will never know.

If you know another modpack in the niche, please tell me so I can swap to it and
stop bothering with this project. As much as I've enjoyed parts of putting it
together, it can be a bother at times. (I'm particularly happy with the pack
icon art, it's my first landscape pixel art and I think it turned out nice).

<enhanced:img src="./IceCreamSundaeIcon.png" alt="mountain sunrise"/>

ps. I've been made aware of some packs that do have that combination, but also
unfortunately feature a significant portion of mods that cross the QoL-hack
boundary; and/or are ill maintained and updated. (not that I have room on that
last point)

To this point I've been using the Complementary or Makeup Ultrafast shaders on
low settings for graphics as I only really care about basic dynamic lighting,
shadows, sunbeams, and distant fog. But I've heard rumor of mods that can meet
their performance with even more biome-specific atmosphere and features. Will be
looking into that shortly.

I'm also considering trying to implement improved nighttime lighting per the
methods used by [Wishbone Games](https://youtu.be/u9X7SHarZQg) as it both makes
nighttime scary and hard to navigate without resorting to an unusable black
screen.
